---
description: WebGL2 and WebGPU TSL shader authoring & disposal guardrails
globs: src/shaders/**
alwaysApply: false
---

- Keep shader files small, modular, and free of hardcoded screen-resolution assumptions (pass `uResolution` / DPR-aware uniforms).
- Prefer Three.js r186+ TSL / `WebGPURenderer`-compatible node materials when targeting WebGPU; keep GLSL fallbacks clean.
- Always dispose compiled `ShaderMaterial`, `BufferGeometry`, and custom `WebGLRenderTarget` instances on scene switch or renderer `dispose()`.
- Verify 0 WebGL/WebGPU shader compilation warnings in browser console via `npm run verify:browser`.
